{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) is a tight-tolerance fit on a part that receives zinc plating (I.Z.B.P.), but the drawing does not state whether the tolerance accounts for plating build-up or if the hole must be re-machined after coating. Uncompensated plating will reduce the bore and can prevent assembly with the mating shaft. The designer should add a note specifying pre-plate machining allowance or post-plate reaming for this feature."

,
"recommended_correction":"Add a note such as 'Hole ⌀16 H7 to be machined after plating' or adjust the pre-plate tolerance to allow for the specified I.Z.B.P. coating thickness."}]}
